        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 3:43PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ</headline>
        <description>At 343 PM MST, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 10
miles south of Miami, or 12 miles southwest of Globe, moving
northwest at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and half inch size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Globe, Superior, Miami, Claypool, Central Heights-Midland City, Top
Of The World, and Inspiration.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
